  "body": "## Summary\nAdds the Grimoire (the agent-facing doctrine Mantle OS follows) and makes its **AppAI chapter the single source of truth** for the assimilation/scanning doctrine \u2014 reflecting that *the egg and assimilation are the same thing*.\n\n### Part 1 \u2014 add the Grimoire under `docs/grimoire/`\n- `THE_GRIMOIRE_CORE_v3_0.md` \u2014 the Core Spellbook (standalone).\n- `GRIMOIRE_APPAI_DOMAIN_v1_0.md` \u2014 the AppAI Domain Extension (NECROMANCY, RESURGERE, \u2026).\n- `README.md` index tying the doctrine to the assimilator code.\n\n### Part 2 \u2014 consolidate the assimilation doctrine into the AppAI chapter\n- **AppAI chapter** gains a new **\"NECROMANCY \u2014 operational detail (the assimilation manual)\"** subsection: the prime directive, the Phase-0 App-Inventory gate + surface\u2192organ table, the 17-phase pipeline, the symbol-role table, the hook runtime + invariants, the hard-fail list, and the APP_INVENTORY template. A **\"One substrate, two casts\"** note makes the egg/RESURGERE \u2194 assimilation/NECROMANCY shared-scanner relationship explicit (one scanner, one `ROLES` table, one `wrappers.py`), with a back-reference from RESURGERE `language_inheritance`.\n- The `language_agnostic` block moves from *proposed* \u2192 **shipped** (references `mantle/assimilator/scanner_ts.py`, the `multilang` extra, and the parity test).\n- **`Mantle_Assimilator.md`** and **`docs/v3/Assimilation_Guide.md`** are reduced to short pointer stubs (kept as valid links + a command cheatsheet) that defer to the AppAI chapter.\n- References repointed in `README.md`, `Mantle_PRIMER.md`, `docs/Mantle_v3_Architecture.md`, `docs/Mantle_Organism_Lens.md`.\n- Doctrine-of-record cross-ref comments added to `scanner.py`, `anchor.py`, `graft.py`, `vault.py` (comments only \u2014 no behavior change).\n\n## Note: the code was already single-source\nInvestigation confirmed there is **no code duplication** \u2014 `mantle/assimilator/scanner.py` is the only scanner/classifier, and `anchor.py`, `graft.py`, and the egg/RESURGERE path (`vault.py` \u2192 `hatchery.incubate`) all reuse it. This PR makes the docs match that reality.\n\n## Dependency\nThe `language_agnostic` \"shipped\" wording references `scanner_ts.py`, introduced in #20. Merge #20 first (or together) so that reference resolves.\n\n## Test plan\n- [x] `python -m mantle audit` \u2014 Stage-1 gate passes\n- [x] `python -m mantle prove` \u2014 68/68 invariants green\n- [x] `python -m mantle assimilate examples/sample_app --dry-run` \u2014 read-only dissection still works (0 host files modified)\n- [x] doctor docs-vs-code coherence check green\n- [x] grep confirms remaining references to the old docs resolve to the stubs (which point onward)\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
